 ### [N-Dimensional Gaussian (6DGS/7DGS)](9230-n-dimensional-gaussian-6dgs-7dgs.md)
-Extends this formulation to model joint distributions over non-spatial dimensions like viewing direction or time, conditioning on queries to derive view-specific or time-specific 3D Gaussians. It differs from standard 3DGS by explicitly encoding dependencies between geometry and observation parameters.
+Extends this formulation to model joint distributions over non-spatial dimensions like viewing direction or time, conditioning on queries to derive view-specific or time-specific 3D Gaussians. Unlike standard 3DGS which treats primitives as static spatial entities, this method explicitly encodes correlations between geometry and appearance/dynamics via cross-covariance terms, allowing for continuous view-dependent effects and temporal coherence without discrete keyframes. Choose it when rendering dynamic or view-dependent scenes requires explicit modeling of non-spatial correlations.
 
